# agent/.env — secrets for the energy agent. NEVER commit the real file (it is gitignored).
#
# ── SINGLE SOURCE OF TRUTH ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The agent RUNS ON THE PI. Production secrets live in ONE place only:
#     energypi.local:~/home-energy-agent/agent/.env
# Rotate/update keys THERE. The Mac's copy of this file is DEV-ONLY (used just for
# running scripts locally) and only needs ANTHROPIC_API_KEY. Editing the Mac's .env
# does NOT change what the running agent uses — that mismatch caused the 2026-07-26
# key-expiry outage. Edit on the Pi:  ssh -t energypi.local nano ~/home-energy-agent/agent/.env
#
# A key committed once is compromised and must be rotated — keep values out of tracked files.
# Full-line `#` comments are fine here; avoid inline comments after a value.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Anthropic API key for the LLM narrative layer (sk-ant-...). The ONE key the Mac's
# dev copy also needs. If it expires, the agent's narrative call fails (control still
# runs; see the LLM try/except hardening).
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Home Assistant — the agent talks to the local HA on the Pi.
HA_URL=http://localhost:8123
# Long-lived access token (HA → Profile → Security → Long-lived access tokens).
HA_TOKEN=

# Tessie — Powerwall control (backup_reserve_percent + mode). Token from tessie.com.
# NOTE: HA ALSO needs this token, as `tessie_bearer` in the Pi's (root-owned)
#   ~/homeassistant/config/secrets.yaml  ->  tessie_bearer: "Bearer <token>"
# because HA's rest_commands can't read .env. So a Tessie rotation touches TWO files
# on the Pi: this .env (agent) and secrets.yaml (HA). configuration.yaml references it
# via `!secret tessie_bearer` — no token inline.
TESSIE_TOKEN=
# Energy site id (an identifier, not a secret).
TESSIE_SITE_ID=

# Optional liveness dead-man's-switch (Healthchecks.io or any ping-URL service). The agent
# pings this on EVERY completed cycle (cheap; finer "last seen" resolution). The ALERT
# threshold is set on the check itself, NOT here — recommended: period 30 min, grace ~2 h
# (tolerates ~4 missed cycles before alerting). Unset = disabled (no-op).
HEALTHCHECK_URL=
